{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circular grass plot 12 feet in diameter is cut by a straight gravel path 3 feet wide, one edge of which passes through the center of the plot. The number of square feet in the remaining grass area is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f39e3c24e36d1f1ec921723129d8935acab6ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 36\\pi-34 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 30\\pi - 15 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 36\\pi - 33 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"377\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1dee9bcddc2cc7af1c8bc1178f843ef684ab293f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ 35\\pi - 9\\sqrt3 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 30\\pi - 9\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"271\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/5270f91d94bb7007e06802cc5dbd0d6b4166ffde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  draw(circle((0,0),6)); draw((-6,0)--(6,0));  pair A=(-5.196,3),B=(5.196,3); draw(A--B--(0,0)--A); draw((0,0)--(0,3)); label(&quot;6&quot;,(-2.598,1.5),SW); label(&quot;3&quot;,(0,1.5),E);  draw((-0.5,3)--(-0.5,2.5)--(0,2.5));  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>The wanted area can be divided into a semicircle and a circular segment.  The area of the semicircle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e38f5b94bc6d412d7ef17a4d882d0ef5888bfff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac12 \\cdot \\pi \\cdot 6^2 = 18\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"117\" height=\"21\" /> square feet.  To find the area of the circular segment, note that by using 30-60-90 triangles (or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>), the chord's length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/8772d61f5af0b70f355caf61084162db9b47f34b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> ft, and the angle of the sector is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fd424e953ac76b50bf6103875acc049d21d3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />.  That means the area of the circular segment is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/25821f63875c9a621471c65926a634c808300cf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\tfrac13 \\cdot \\pi \\cdot 6^2) - (\\tfrac12 \\cdot 6\\sqrt{3} \\cdot 3) = 12\\pi - 9\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"303\" height=\"23\" /> square feet.  Thus, the area of the remaining grassy area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/765e456cb1a57ce3bfc5041892b2657cc9e97a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 30\\pi - 9\\sqrt3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"129\" height=\"33\" /> square feet.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\"